   383	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   384	    """
   385	    Fill hollow sprites from a reversed edge legend, then remove that legend strip.
   386	
   387	    Input structure:
   388	    - The outer border is mostly background, while one side contains a compact 2xN or Nx2 palette inside the removable edge band.
   389	    - Hollow single-color sprites live away from that band; some of their border colors are encoded by the legend and one sprite may be a distractor.
   390	    - Unlike the original family, the border-key colors are on the inward line of the palette and the fill colors are on the edge-touching line.
   391	
   392	    Rule:
   393	    - Detect the palette side, decode each pair using the opposite reading direction for that side, and build a border-color to fill-color mapping from the inward line to the outward line.
   394	    - Fill every enclosed background hole whose dominant surrounding border color appears in that mapping.
   395	    - After filling on the full grid, crop away the entire 2-row or 2-column side strip that hosted the palette.
   396	
   397	    Key insight: The palette is both misleading and disposable. Its useful color keys sit on the inner line rather than the edge line, and once those reversed instructions are used, the whole palette strip disappears from the output.
   398	    """
   399	    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
   400	    bg = _bg_boundary(g)
   401	
   402	    mapping, pal_mask, (side, _start, _end) = _combo_palette_mapping(g, bg)
   403	    assert mapping, "main: palette mapping must be non-empty"
   404	    return _solve_with_mapping(g, bg, mapping, pal_mask, side)
   405	
